---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Sustainabox – Aim Higher">

	<!-- Hero -->
	<header class="hero">
		<div class="hero-overlay">
			<div class="hero-content">
				<h1>Sustainabox</h1>
				<p class="hero-tagline">Aim Higher</p>
				<p class="hero-sub">We're building more than a house. This is our journey into sustainable living, mobile freedom, and hands-on learning.</p>
				<a href="#specs" class="btn btn-primary">Explore the Build</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</header>

	<!-- Specifications -->
	<section id="specs">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>The Build</h2>
			<p>Sustainabox is a custom container home built from one 20-foot and two 40-foot high-cube (HC) one-trip shipping containers. Set on pier foundations and connected by a deck to create a courtyard, the layout balances comfort, function, and adaptability.</p>
			<p>We're using a combination of detailed SketchUp models, hand-drawn diagrams, and site surveys to guide the build and coordinate with trades.</p>

			<div class="container-grid">
				<div class="container-card">
					<div class="container-label">C1</div>
					<h3>Container 1</h3>
					<p class="container-size">40-foot HC one-trip</p>
					<p>Main living space with kitchen, living room, and 1/2 bathroom. Sits at the rear of the build site, parallel to the road.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="container-card">
					<div class="container-label">C2</div>
					<h3>Container 2</h3>
					<p class="container-size">40-foot HC one-trip</p>
					<p>Positioned to the right side and connected with C1 at the rear left corner. Houses two bedrooms, a full bathroom, and a utility space with washer/dryer.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="container-card">
					<div class="container-label">C3</div>
					<h3>Container 3</h3>
					<p class="container-size">20-foot HC one-trip</p>
					<p>Parallel to C2 on the left side. A flex space — office, guest room, and storage. Power and AC, no plumbing. Sits separately from the main layout.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Drawings -->
	<section id="drawings" class="section-alt">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>Drawings</h2>
			<p>These drawings include a mix of exports from our SketchUp 3D model and hand-drawn details. We update this section as the design evolves and as trades provide input.</p>

			<h3>Survey</h3>
			<p>The survey was provided during the property purchase and shows the full lot, including the small piece of land that was added years ago and officially merged into the parcel. It captures early topographic details and key landmarks, such as the original wood shed, which has since been removed. The entire foundation and container placement were aligned around this feature.</p>
			<div class="gallery">
				<img src="/images/Survey-1-1.jpg" alt="Full property survey" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Survey-2-1.jpg" alt="Survey detail - lot boundaries" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Survey-3-1.jpg" alt="Survey detail - topographic features" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Survey-4-1.jpg" alt="Survey detail - landmarks" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Survey-5-1.jpg" alt="Survey detail - elevation notes" loading="lazy" />
			</div>
			<div class="download-group">
				<a href="/pdfs/Survey.pdf" class="btn btn-outline" download>Download Survey</a>
			</div>

			<h3>Topo Survey</h3>
			<p>The topo survey focuses on the main portion of the lot. It provided the critical elevation data used to determine initial pier heights and to ensure proper leveling across the site. The goal is to place the front of the deck approximately one foot above grade.</p>
			<div class="gallery">
				<img src="/images/Topo-1-1.jpg" alt="Topographic survey overview" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Topo-2-1.jpg" alt="Topo survey - contour lines" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Topo-3-1.jpg" alt="Topo survey - elevation data" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Topo-4-1.jpg" alt="Topo survey - reference points" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Topo-5-1.jpg" alt="Topo survey - site boundaries" loading="lazy" />
			</div>
			<div class="download-group">
				<a href="/pdfs/Allstar-survey-16200-Monks-Mountain-dr-2.pdf" class="btn btn-outline" download>Download Topo Survey</a>
			</div>

			<h3>Elevation</h3>
			<p>The elevation views were generated using geospatial mapping tools within SketchUp, pulling real-world terrain data and surrounding structures into the model. This tool has been incredibly useful for visualizing how the containers sit on the land.</p>
			<div class="gallery">
				<img src="/images/Elevation-1-1.jpg" alt="Elevation view - front" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Elevation-2-2.jpg" alt="Elevation view - aerial perspective" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Elevation-2-3.jpg" alt="Elevation view - side angle" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Elevation-3-2.jpg" alt="Elevation view - rear" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Elevation-4.jpg" alt="Elevation view - landscape context" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Elevation-5-1.jpg" alt="Elevation view - with terrain" loading="lazy" />
			</div>

			<h3>Septic</h3>
			<p>The septic system layout was designed to meet county requirements and is placed in the rear portion of the lot. The placement was finalized with input from the topo survey and soil conditions.</p>
			<div class="gallery">
				<img src="/images/Septic-1-1.jpg" alt="Septic system layout" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Septic-2.jpg" alt="Septic plan detail" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Septic-3-1.jpg" alt="Septic drain field placement" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Septic-4.jpg" alt="Septic system specifications" loading="lazy" />
			</div>
			<div class="download-group">
				<a href="/pdfs/16200-Monks-Mountain-PRELIM2.pdf" class="btn btn-outline" download>Download Septic Plan</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Foundation -->
	<section id="foundation">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>Foundation</h2>
			<p>The Sustainabox foundation is built using reinforced concrete piers designed to support the weight and structural demands of C1 and C2. C3 will have a temporary foundation.</p>

			<div class="gallery">
				<img src="/images/Foundation-5-1.jpg" alt="Foundation pier layout" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Foundation-2.jpg" alt="Pier construction detail" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Foundation-3.jpg" alt="Foundation reinforcement" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Split-View-1.jpg" alt="Split view - foundation and structure" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Pier-Detail.png" alt="Widened pier detail at C1/C2 junction" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/engineering-1.png" alt="Structural engineering specifications" loading="lazy" />
			</div>

			<div class="download-group">
				<a href="/pdfs/25251-16200-Monks-Mountain-Dr-08-25-25.pdf" class="btn btn-outline" download>Download Structural Engineering Plan</a>
			</div>

			<div class="specs-box">
				<h3>Codes & Specifications</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>2021 International Residential Code</li>
					<li>ASCE 7-16 Minimum Design Loads</li>
					<li>BRAB Report #33: Residential Slab-on-Ground</li>
					<li>ACI 301-05 / ACI-318-08 Structural Concrete</li>
				</ul>
			</div>

			<div class="specs-box">
				<h3>Concrete Specifications</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>Min compressive strength: 3000 PSI (foundation) / 4000 PSI (pool)</li>
					<li>Min cement content: 4.5 sacks/c.y.</li>
					<li>Max water/cement ratio: 0.48</li>
					<li>Slump range: 5" min – 8" max</li>
					<li>Max coarse aggregate size: 3/4"</li>
					<li>All reinforcing: ASTM A-615, Grade 60</li>
				</ul>
			</div>

			<p>The widened pier at the shared corner where C1 and C2 meet is expanded to 24x24 inches with solid grout fill and vertical rebar, ensuring structural integrity at one of the most critical load points.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Interior -->
	<section id="interior" class="section-alt">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>Interior</h2>
			<p>C1 and C2 will be framed with metal studs, insulated using closed-cell spray foam, and finished with drywall. Container 3 will take a simpler approach with plywood walls and no plumbing.</p>

			<div class="gallery">
				<img src="/images/Interior-1-1.jpg" alt="Full compound overhead view" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Interior-2-1.jpg" alt="C2 - bedrooms, bathroom, utility" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Interior-3-1.jpg" alt="C1 - kitchen and living area" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Interior-4-1.jpg" alt="Interior layout flow" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Interior-Kitchen-Container-3.jpg" alt="Kitchen detail" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Interior-20ft-2.jpg" alt="C3 - flex space interior" loading="lazy" />
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Systems -->
	<section id="systems">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>Systems</h2>

			<h3>Electrical</h3>
			<p>The electrical plans outline key circuits for each container, including dedicated runs for major appliances, lighting, switches, outlets, and utility connections. C3 will have a simplified 120V layout pending final AC requirements.</p>
			<div class="gallery">
				<img src="/images/Electrical-Plan-Main-Living-Contatiner.jpg" alt="Electrical plan - C1 main living" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/Electrical-Plan-Bedroom-Utility-Container.jpg" alt="Electrical plan - C2 bedrooms/utility" loading="lazy" />
				<img src="/images/20-ft-container.jpg" alt="C3 electrical layout" loading="lazy" />
			</div>

			<h3>Plumbing</h3>
			<p>The plumbing layout covers fixture locations, supply and drain lines, and utility connections. C1 includes the kitchen, half bathroom, and tie-ins for hot water and filtration. C2 includes the main bathroom and laundry/utility connections.</p>
			<div class="gallery">
				<img src="/images/Plumbing.jpg" alt="Plumbing layout plan" loading="lazy" />
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- C3 Delivery -->
	<section class="section-dark">
		<div class="container" style="text-align: center;">
			<h2>C3 Has Arrived</h2>
			<p>Check out the delivery of Container 3! It's already on site to serve as storage throughout the build, sitting on a temporary foundation.</p>
			<div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 2rem auto 0;">
				<img src="/images/Lake.jpg" alt="Container 3 delivery and site view" style="border-radius: 12px;" loading="lazy" />
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Contact -->
	<section id="contact">
		<div class="container contact-section">
			<h2>Get in Touch</h2>
			<p>Right now, this contact info is mainly for those helping us bring Sustainabox to life — trades, suppliers, and curious friends.</p>
			<p>But soon, we'll use it to help guests plan stays, book experiences, and connect with everything this space has to offer.</p>
			<div class="contact-emails">
				<a href="mailto:jenswid@outlook.com" class="btn btn-outline">jenswid@outlook.com</a>
				<a href="mailto:codyswid@outlook.com" class="btn btn-outline">codyswid@outlook.com</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Lightbox -->
	<div class="lightbox" id="lightbox">
		<img src="" alt="" />
	</div>

	<script>
		const lightbox = document.getElementById('lightbox');
		const lbImg = lightbox?.querySelector('img');

		document.querySelectorAll('.gallery img').forEach(img => {
			img.addEventListener('click', () => {
				if (lbImg && lightbox) {
					lbImg.src = img.src;
					lbImg.alt = img.alt;
					lightbox.classList.add('active');
				}
			});
		});

		lightbox?.addEventListener('click', () => {
			lightbox.classList.remove('active');
		});

		document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
			if (e.key === 'Escape') lightbox?.classList.remove('active');
		});
	</script>

</Layout>

<style>
	/* Hero */
	.hero {
		background: url('/images/Elevation-2-2.jpg') center/cover no-repeat;
		min-height: 80vh;
		position: relative;
	}

	.hero-overlay {
		background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(26,39,68,0.85), rgba(44,82,130,0.7));
		min-height: 80vh;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
	}

	.hero-content {
		text-align: center;
		color: white;
		padding: 2rem;
		max-width: 700px;
	}

	.hero h1 {
		font-size: 4rem;
		color: white;
		margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
	}

	.hero-tagline {
		font-family: var(--font-heading);
		font-size: 1.5rem;
		font-weight: 400;
		opacity: 0.9;
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
		font-style: italic;
	}

	.hero-sub {
		font-size: 1.15rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
		opacity: 0.95;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	/* Container cards */
	.container-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
		gap: 1.5rem;
		margin-top: 2.5rem;
	}

	.container-card {
		background: var(--color-warm);
		border-radius: 12px;
		padding: 2rem;
		border-left: 4px solid var(--color-blue);
	}

	.container-label {
		font-family: var(--font-heading);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--color-blue);
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}

	.container-size {
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		color: var(--color-muted);
		font-weight: 500;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}

	/* Specs boxes */
	.specs-box {
		background: var(--color-warm);
		border-radius: 12px;
		padding: 2rem;
		margin: 2rem 0;
	}

	.specs-box ul {
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
	}

	.specs-box li {
		padding: 0.4rem 0;
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
		position: relative;
		font-size: 0.95rem;
	}

	.specs-box li::before {
		content: "▪";
		position: absolute;
		left: 0;
		color: var(--color-blue);
	}

	/* Contact */
	.contact-section {
		text-align: center;
		max-width: 600px;
	}

	.contact-emails {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 1rem;
		justify-content: center;
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
	}

	@media (max-width: 768px) {
		.hero h1 {
			font-size: 2.5rem;
		}

		.hero-tagline {
			font-size: 1.2rem;
		}

		.container-grid {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
